---
import StoryLayout from '../../layouts/StoryLayout.astro';
import stories from '../../data/stories.json';

const story = stories.find(s => s.slug === 'interpath-neoantigen-phase3')!;
---

<style is:global>
  .phantom-wrap { width: 100%; margin: 0; line-height: 0; }
  .interpath-neoantigen-phase3-canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 380px; background: var(--bg); }

  /* Story-scoped text tokens.
     --inp-dim  : darker than --muted so small text clears WCAG AA on --surface2 (4.9:1)
     --inp-warn : darker than --accent-red so "not disclosed" text clears AA on cream (5.6:1+) */
  .inp-select-panel,
  .inp-trial-diagram,
  .inp-term-audit {
    --inp-dim: #5f5a4e;
    --inp-warn: #a01b1b;
  }

  /* === REENACTMENT #1: THE SELECTION PANEL === */
  .inp-select-panel {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: 'SF Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .inp-select-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
  }
  .inp-select-count {
    color: var(--story);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .inp-select-list {
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    max-height: 260px;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }
  .inp-mutation-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .inp-mutation-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .inp-mutation-name { color: var(--text); }
  .inp-mutation-type { font-size: 0.65rem; color: var(--inp-dim); }
  .inp-select-divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--story);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .inp-select-output {
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .inp-output-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--story);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .inp-selected-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .inp-selected-tag {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--story) 12%, var(--bg));
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--story) 35%, var(--bg));
    color: var(--story);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .inp-select-footer {
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    font-style: italic;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  /* === REENACTMENT #2: TRIAL ARCHITECTURE === */
  .inp-trial-diagram {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    font-family: 'SF Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .inp-trial-diagram { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .inp-trial-arm {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  /* No opacity on the ghost arm — colours are dimmed explicitly so text
     contrast is computable and stays above 4.5:1. */
  .inp-trial-arm.inp-ghost {
    border-style: dashed;
    border-color: var(--border-hover);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .inp-arm-header {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--story);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .inp-ghost .inp-arm-header { color: var(--inp-dim); }
  .inp-arm-title {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .inp-ghost .inp-arm-title { color: var(--inp-dim); }
  .inp-arm-detail {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .inp-ghost .inp-arm-detail { color: var(--inp-dim); }
  .inp-arm-bracket {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border-hover);
    padding-left: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .inp-ghost .inp-arm-bracket {
    border-left-style: dashed;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
  }
  .inp-trial-endpoint {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    background: var(--surface2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .inp-endpoint-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .inp-endpoint-result {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--story);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .inp-endpoint-numbers {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--inp-warn);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .inp-trial-footer {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .inp-trial-footer em {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  /* === REENACTMENT #3: TERMINOLOGY AUDIT === */
  .inp-term-audit {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-family: 'SF Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .inp-term-audit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .inp-term-col { padding: 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .inp-term-col:first-child {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .inp-term-col:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  }
  .inp-term-col:last-child { background: var(--bg); }
  .inp-term-header {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .inp-term-col:first-child .inp-term-header { color: var(--story); }
  .inp-term-col:last-child .inp-term-header { color: var(--inp-warn); }
  .inp-term-item {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .inp-term-col:first-child .inp-term-item { color: var(--text); }
  .inp-term-col:first-child .inp-term-item::before {
    content: '\25CF';
    color: var(--story);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
  }
  .inp-term-col:last-child .inp-term-item {
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border-hover);
  }
  .inp-term-col:last-child .inp-term-item::before {
    content: '\25CB';
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .inp-term-scope {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--inp-dim);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>

<StoryLayout story={story}>
  <div class="container">

    <section class="section" id="selection-problem">
      <h2><span class="num">01 — The Problem</span>The Selection Problem</h2>
      <p>A typical melanoma tumor carries roughly 489 nonsynonymous mutations. The vaccine can target up to 34. An algorithm no one outside two companies can examine makes the cut.</p>
      <p>Melanoma is among the most mutation-rich cancers in humans. Whole-exome sequencing of melanoma tumors reveals a median of approximately 12 mutations per megabase of coding DNA, with an average of 489 nonsynonymous mutations per tumor — changes in the DNA that alter a protein's structure. The range is vast: some tumors carry as few as 45, others more than 800. Each mutation is a potential signal. Each produces a protein fragment — a neoantigen — that exists only in the patient's cancer cells, not in their healthy tissue. A vaccine built to encode those neoantigens could, in theory, train the patient's immune system to hunt and destroy any cell displaying them.</p>
      <p>The challenge is selection. The therapy developed by Moderna and Merck — intismeran autogene, formerly mRNA-4157/V940 — encodes up to 34 neoantigens per patient, delivered as synthetic mRNA in a lipid nanoparticle. Thirty-four out of roughly 489. That ratio means someone, or something, must decide which mutations matter most, which are most likely to provoke an immune response, and which to discard. The selection is the personalization. Without it, you have a platform. With it, you have a therapy designed for one person's cancer.</p>
      <p>Moderna describes this selector on its corporate blog as "a proprietary algorithm developed in collaboration with Merck" that "reviews these mutations and predicts up to 34 of those mutations that are believed to help the study participant's immune system better recognize tumor cells and to launch an attack." The algorithm takes in the patient's whole-exome and transcriptome sequencing data, along with their HLA genotype, and outputs the neoantigen payload.</p>
      <p>The only peer-reviewed characterization of this algorithm is AACR 2020 Abstract 6539, which calls it the "bioinformatics algorithm of mRNA-4157." The abstract, published six years ago, describes a test performed by Moderna's own team on sequencing data from 29 colorectal cancer patients shared by the National Cancer Institute. The algorithm captured 41% of neoantigens that were confirmed to be recognized by the patients' own tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes. For 61% of patients, at least one reactive neoantigen was included in the vaccine the algorithm designed. The abstract does not describe the algorithm's architecture, training data, or validation methodology. No independent third-party evaluation has been published. Whether the algorithm uses machine learning techniques or conventional bioinformatics tools — HLA binding prediction, expression filtering, clonality weighting — is, based on the public record, an open question. No sponsor or peer-reviewed source applies the label "AI" or "machine learning" to this selector.</p>
      <p>That 2020 characterization is now six years old. The algorithm may have been substantially modified since. Its current performance is unknown.</p>

